ies anarchist cities  as part of that  soup uh but i don't think like on that  alone people are going to make up their  minds but no you know when you talk  about people who are undecided at this  point  i don't i don't know like what are they  even voting on like what is going to be  the issue that drives them because  they're undecided to begin with  so it's like hard to put yourself in  their heads to begin with what i've been  looking at for this friday show segment  is that those voters ultimately tend to  either vote on  their general impression of how the  economy is doing and their general  impression may not be accurate  but their general impression of how the  economy is doing and what is described  as a  gut feeling so it doesn't seem like with  that in mind  a justice department declaration about  anarchist cities is going to be what  changes their mind  yeah that kind of goes back to that  conversation about how this election  will be decided by meta issues that's  what alan lichtman talks about right how  it's really going to come down to the  coronavirus and the economy and yeah  there's a lot of like gut feeling that's  wrapped up in both of those things  um so yeah i do still think that the  fundamentals of this  uh race are going to be about those two  issues  now you have the supreme court situation  too maybe that's going to play a bit of  a factor but i think it's ultimately  going to be mainly coronavirus and the  economy  we will be here with you including this  coming tuesday night september 29th  the first debate assuming it doesn't get  cancelled between donald trump and  joseph r biden jr  we will be starting our coverage at 8 30  p.m on the east  5 30 p.m in the west and it is going to  be  a great coming together hopefully of our  audience and we will have so much to  discuss  but before then we'll have new shows and  bonus shows all of this week  the david pakman show at davidpakman.com  [Music]
 

